    "result_text": "The build passes. The implementation is complete and green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `birthDate` \u2192 `ageBand` derivation for owner creation/retrieval. The endpoint is `POST /api/owners` (create) and `GET /api/owners/{ownerId}` (read-back), both driven by OfficeFloor function pipelines mapping through the MapStruct `OwnerMapper` and OpenAPI-generated DTOs.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`**\n   - Added optional `birthDate` (`format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` request schema so requests bind it.\n   - Added read-only `ageBand` (string) to the `Owner` response schema.\n\n2. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a `birthDate` `LocalDate` field (mapped to a `birth_date DATE` column) with getter/setter, so the value is persisted and available at GET time.\n\n3. **Database schemas** \u2014 added `birth_date DATE` to the `owners` table in the hsqldb, h2, mysql, and postgres schemas, and appended the trailing `NULL` to the hsqldb seed inserts (which use positional `VALUES`). h2/postgres seed data use explicit column lists and needed no change.\n\n4. **`AgeBand` helper** (new) \u2014 computes full-years between `birthDate` and `registrationDate` (`Period.between`), returning `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), `SENIOR` (65+), or `null` when no birth date was supplied.\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"ageBand\", expression = \"\u2026AgeBand.of(owner)\")`; `birthDate` maps by name automatically in both directions.\n\nThe age band is computed against `registrationDate` (not `now()`) as specified. The acceptance test `coreDerivesAgeBand` passes (birthDate `1990-01-01`, registrationDate `2026-09-07` \u2192 `ADULT`), and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures/errors).\n\nOne thing worth flagging: the pre-existing `db/mysql/data.sql` owner inserts already used a positional `VALUES` list with fewer values than the table's columns before my change, so it was already inconsistent with its schema \u2014 I left it as-is since MySQL isn't used by the tests, but you may want to reconcile it separately.",
